2. ውዳሴ ማርያም (WUDASE MARYAM) AND ጸሎት ዘዘወትር
   Source: https://github.com/tecleet/wudase-mariam (no licence stated)
   The underlying prayer is centuries-old, public-domain Ethiopian Orthodox
   liturgical text; this particular digitisation is credited to that repository
   and reshaped into stanzas by tools/build_wudase.py. If you hold rights to
   that transcription and want it removed or re-credited, please open an issue.

3. ስንክሳር (SYNAXARIUM)
   Amharic synaxarium text, drawn from two sources:
     * The gitsaweandsinksarbot project by hailemariam-eyayu
       (https://github.com/hailemariam-eyayu/gitsaweandsinksarbot),
       normalized by tools/extract_sinksar.py.
     * The Nexuss0781/synaxarium dataset on the Hugging Face Hub
       (https://huggingface.co/datasets/Nexuss0781/synaxarium), tagged
       MIT License, normalized by tools/extract_sinksar_hf.py (the current
       source of the bundled text). The MIT permission notice is reproduced
       in the app's Licenses & sources screen.
   The underlying commemorations are traditional Ethiopian Orthodox
   liturgical content.

4. ግጻዌ (GITSAWE)
   The lectionary (the fixed 366-day cycle plus the movable, Sunday,
   Athanasius, and Bahre Hasab collections) was scanned and transcribed from
   the printed ግጻዌ by the Sinq maintainer, who releases it as open content
   under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 — the same terms as the bundled Bible text. The
   underlying lectionary is traditional Ethiopian Orthodox liturgical
   material.

